# WolkaraForever layer patch 0063 - mobile interface: a drag around the spell wheel turns it
#
# Why: the WolkaraRoue spell wheel sits in a ring around the screen's bottom-right corner.
# In combat the game lets an add-on move its spell buttons only in answer to a click or a
# mouse wheel, never to a drag, so a finger could not spin it in a fight. A finger that comes
# down on that ring and moves is now sent as wheel notches - one per spell, 18 degrees of
# travel around the corner - with the pointer resting where the finger came down, which is
# where the wheel listens. A flick keeps turning for a moment after the finger lifts. A tap
# there is still a tap and a hold still a right click; only a drag changes. Each notch ticks
# the phone's haptics unless the touch controls' Haptics switch is off.
#
# Gated: direct touch in the mobile interface only, and WolkaraForeverWheelDragV1 = NO turns
# it off and gives the corner back to the camera.
#
# Applies to: translation/AppKit/AppKit.m (after 0055).
# Upstream: no (it serves one add-on's layout).
#
diff --git a/translation/AppKit/AppKit.m b/translation/AppKit/AppKit.m
index 32095d0..d8cd487 100644
--- a/translation/AppKit/AppKit.m
+++ b/translation/AppKit/AppKit.m
